Service Fabric classic V1 component translations and source ledger
-----------------------------------------------------------------

The source-derived acceptance scenarios and selected native test expectations
documented in docs/features/kuberic/sf-v1-port-ledger.md derive from Microsoft
Service Fabric at commit 3988b4518236d2d0a37f4d8bdcdf0a2093c5a61d.

The internal Rust OperationQueue and its component tests in
kuberic-runtime/src/replicator/v1/operation_queue.rs and
kuberic-runtime/src/replicator/v1/operation_queue/tests.rs translate selected
Microsoft OperationQueue.h/.cpp algorithms and OperationQueue.Test.cpp
assertions at that same pin, with Rust ownership/storage adaptations and
additional production-source-derived cases. They are not factory-selected.

The internal sender.rs, ack.rs, session.rs and their component tests under
kuberic-runtime/src/replicator/v1/ translate selected ReliableOperationSender,
AckSender, RemoteSession and ReplicationSession production algorithms and
ReliableOperationSender.Test.cpp/DecayAverage.Test.cpp assertions. The sender
also translates DecayAverage and the REPerformanceCounters tick-mean helper.
This is a bounded session responsibility port, not copy/build/primary/receiver
integration or a carrier. Rust ownership, staged effects and injected time
replace native pointer/timer execution; components remain production-unselected.

The private transport.rs, buffers.rs, async_runtime.rs, sf_v1.proto and their
component tests adapt selected ReplicationTransport message contracts,
ReplicationEndpointId routing, RemoteSession send outcomes, and
ReliableOperationSender/AckSender timer-lifetime obligations at the same pin.
Tokio/tonic, bounded Rust queues and explicit versioned buffer framing replace
native execution/transport representations. No native wire serialization,
Common/Transport timer library, test harness or activated listener is imported.
See the provenance register for exact selected ranges and remaining owners.

The private replication_queue_manager.rs, replica_manager.rs and their component
tests under kuberic-runtime/src/replicator/v1/ translate selected
ReplicationQueueManager/ReplicaManager primary queue, configured quorum,
assignment/completion and catch-up algorithms, plus selected
ReplicaManager.Test.cpp expectations at the same pin. Rust-owned queue entries,
caller-established sessions, staged effects and separate completion receivers
replace COM operations/job queues; they do not import native utilities or
implement the complete primary, copy/build, slow-fault or role state machines.
The components remain production-unselected.

